Maintainer wish, 2026-11-24. Part of k224; pairs with k230 (the setup skill).

When a project has no CLAUDE.md, `unreagent init` writes a starter one. It never overwrites an existing file, and `init -check` writes nothing and reports it as a finding.

Content of the starter:
1. The facts that are the same in every unreagent project: the launcher supervises the editor, how to build and restart (pointing at the unreagent-build and unreagent-iterate skills), that skills come through the `skills` tool.
2. A kickstart block, clearly marked as temporary: this project is not described yet; ask the user about it (genre and scope, target platforms, C++ versus Blueprint policy, source control), write the answers into this file, then remove this block. Once k230 ships, the block names that skill.

Maintainer wording: put into the empty CLAUDE.md something like "ask the user for more information about the project and update CLAUDE.md", so the agent starts out asking.

Open, main agent proposal (not the maintainer decision): only `init` writes the file; a plain start without a config writes nothing into the project. No agents or roles are written by the launcher.

Done when: init on a project without CLAUDE.md writes the starter and says so in its output; a second run and a project with its own CLAUDE.md are left alone; -check writes nothing; pinned by tests; README quick start mentions it. Owner: unreagent-worker (cmd/launcher/init.go), text reviewed by unreagent-skill-author; README by unreagent-doc-writer. Runs after k251 (same file).

